  "title": "A Good Year For The Pv Eth In 2014",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Retired Members' Association PV ETH",
      "text": "The programme of events organised by the Association for Retired Members of ETH Zurich (Vereinigung der Pensionierten der ETH Zürich, PV ETH) is designed to ensure that former employees at ETH Zurich keep in touch with each other and with the university after they have retired. The annual programme generally comprises about four slide shows, 13 walks and visits, one or two coach trips, the Chlausfeier (St Nicholas’s Day party) and the Annual General Meeting.\n\nThis year the AGM took place on 5 March at the Hotel Kronenhof in Zurich. It was attended by 71 members and one guest.\n\nChairwoman Karin Schram said that the PV ETH can look back on a good year in 2014:"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "Souvenir from Nussbüel in the canton of Glarus. (Photo: Beat Rüedin)"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Retired Members' Association PV ETH",
      "text": "The Retired Members' Association PV ETH was founded on 25 March 1976 by retired employees of ETH Zurich with the aim of promoting and maintaining friendly relations between former members of ETH Zurich and its four research institutes by organising social and cultural events."
    }
  ],
